.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
node_modules/
# Local agent workspace. Holds git worktrees, and a skills symlink that points at an
# absolute path outside this repository — committing it would give every other clone
# a dangling link. The page style kit it references is documented in site/README.md.
.claude/
# site/data/ is built, never committed. It used to be committed and hash-gated, which
# needed the gate to answer "are these bytes what the pipeline produces?" — and that
# question has no stable answer, because the build is byte-reproducible on one machine
# but not across platforms (panels/NPEV.json and panels/all.json differ between macOS
# and the Linux runner; everything else reproduces). Building it in CI instead leaves
# one builder, so there is nothing to fall out of sync and nothing to re-stamp.
# site/dist/ is covered by `dist/`.
site/data/
# Probe leftovers. sandbox.py deliberately does not guard os.mkfifo/os.mknod (see
# docs/review-backlog.md B12), so exercising that gap plants a node inside final/.
# git skips non-regular files, so one never shows up as untracked no matter what
# flags you pass — it just sits in the release tree looking like data. Naming it
# here does not make git see it, but it does tell a reader the name is expected.
evgc-probe-fifo
